Dear Editor,

We are submitting our manuscript titled "Vupr-QLI: Complex Coherence Projection for Interpretable Network Intrusion Detection" for consideration in Pattern Recognition.

**Novelty and Significance:** We propose a new mathematical framework that replaces linear PCA with a quantum-inspired complex projection. Our method, Vupr-QLI, achieves 0.947 AUC on CICIDS2017, outperforming PCA+Logistic Regression by 3.5 points while providing feature-level interpretability via the magnitude-phase map of coherence vectors. This addresses the critical trade-off between accuracy and interpretability in security applications.

**Reproducibility:** Full source code, including random seeds and environment details, is publicly available at https://github.com/Vupr-QLI/Vupr-QLI-CICIDS2017 to ensure complete reproducibility of all results.

**Suitability for Pattern Recognition:** The work aligns with the journal's focus on novel pattern recognition methodologies with mathematical rigor and significant experimental validation on real-world data.

We confirm that this manuscript is original, has not been published elsewhere, and is not under consideration by another journal. All authors have approved the manuscript and agree with its submission.

Thank you for your consideration. We look forward to your response.

